  "id": 477,
  "description": "Next Element Wisdom Builders\n\n This guild is designed to give new players a chance to join a guild and learn some of the guild mechanics before moving on to their forever guild.\n\nThis is not a guild for alternate characters. It is for new players only.\n \nUnlike other guilds, N.E.W.B. implements a maximum level requirement, afterwhich players must move on to a higher level guild of their choosing. \n\nMembers who reach a combat level of 40, or a total level of 400, which ever comes first, must leave the guild to make room for other new players to have a chance to join the guild. Additionally, inactive players will be dismissed for the same reason.\n Anyone who reaches CL40 or TL400 and does not leave will also be dismissed.\n \nThere is no obligation to participate in raids or challenges for any members, but members are encouraged to do so in order to learn how guild functions work.\n\nMembers may be permitted to stay a little longer if there are no valid applications to the guild.\n\nIf you are dismissed from the guild prematurely it was likely for inactivity, reapplying to the guild when returning to the game is permitted.\n\n~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ -\nContributing to challenges will yield Exp for the guild as well as personal Guild Mastery Exp for you. Completed challenges will earn &#039;Marks&#039; for the guild which can be used to initiate guild raids.\n\nParticipating in guild raids will earn both Combat Experience and Guild Mastery Experience.\n\n~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~ - ~   - ~ - ~ - ~ -\n Raids will be set at 1:00 pm amd 5:00 pm EST if we have enough marks. \n\nMembers dismissal will be temporarily suspended when there are enough marks for a raid to assure that members contribution to challenges are rewarded with raid participation. \n \n There is currently no guild discord.",
